# supercronic crontab for the receipt-index scheduler container.
#
# Mounted read-only at /app/crontab; the compose `scheduler` service overrides
# the image ENTRYPOINT with `supercronic /app/crontab`.
#
# Ingest isn't here. It runs all the time in the compose `ingest` service
# (`receipt-index serve`). A `receipt-index ingest` line added back by mistake
# would find each source's lock held by serve and exit 3 on every tick, so it
# can't race it.
#
# Notes:
#   * supercronic will not start a job while its previous run is still going —
#     no-overlap is the default, per job line.
#   * No environment is declared here. supercronic does not scrub the
#     environment before running jobs, so everything from the compose
#     `env_file` / `environment` (DATABASE_URL, RECEIPT_INDEX_CONFIG, ...) is
#     already visible to these commands.
#   * Job stdout/stderr goes to the container log.
#   * Schedules are in the container's timezone, which is UTC unless TZ is set
#     in the compose environment. Only the two backup lines care.
#   * Commands run under /bin/sh -c (supercronic's default; it takes no `%`
#     shortcuts — see deploy/backup.sh).
#   * The two mirror lines are offset from each other and from the backups.
#     No-overlap is per line, so a long mirror can still run through another
#     line's tick.

# Mirror rendered receipts to Dropbox. `copy` is additive: it never deletes at
# the destination. The store writes each file to a `.tmp` name first, so those
# are skipped.
7,22,37,52 * * * * rclone copy /app/data/receipts dropbox:receipt-index/receipts --exclude "*.tmp" --config /app/.rclone/rclone.conf -v

# Mirror the rotating database dumps. Same additive semantics; the fixed set of
# 7 day-of-week and 12 month filenames is what bounds the destination.
12,27,42,57 * * * * rclone copy /app/data/backups dropbox:receipt-index/backups --exclude "*.tmp" --config /app/.rclone/rclone.conf -v

# Nightly database dump, day-of-week rotation (7 files).
17 3 * * * /app/backup.sh

# Monthly database dump on the 1st, month-name rotation (12 files). Offset from
# the nightly line, since no-overlap is per line and the two would otherwise
# dump at the same moment.
47 3 1 * * /app/backup.sh monthly
